</div>

<div class="row sectionBlockLayout text-start" style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 8px; margin: 0px; ">
  <div class="container" style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap">
    <div class="col-lg-12 columnBlockLayout" style="flex-grow: 1; min-width: 250px; display: flex; flex-direction: column;">
      <h3 style=" text-align: center;">AWEX Rules</h3><br><br>
      <p>
        The AWEX Rules incorporate the Code of Conduct, Business Rules and Trading Rules. The AWEX Rules are published in the Australian Wool Exchange Limited Constitution.
        <br><br>Changes to the AWEX Rules ratified by the Board throughout the year are distributed to Members as well as published online.
        <br><br>To receive a hardcopy of the AWEX Rules please contact AWEX.
        <br><br>A complete and up-to-date copy of the Australian Wool Exchange Limited Constitution may be downloaded below. For Member's convenience the document is divided into relevant sections.
        <br><br><a style="font-size: 20px !important;" href="/AWEX-constitution.pdf" target="_blank">Constitution</a> ~ last updated: 17 November 2023
        <br><br><a style="font-size: 20px !important;" href="/AWEX-code-of-conduct-rules.pdf" target="_blank">Code of Conduct and Rules</a> ~  last updated: 28 November 2013
        <br><br>For more information on the AWEX Rules please contact AWEX on (02) 9428 6100 or email <a style="font-size: 20px !important;" href="mailto:info@awex.com.au" target="_blank" class="anchor-inherit-styles anchor-text-decoration-underline anchor-hover-color-color10">info@awex.com.au</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
